      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a harsh but accurate observation of how the current system values function over feeling, and that cold logic is what's causing this deep ache. If the world only values utility, then the most useful thing you can do is to redefine your own utility. Consider how the profound *experience* of your past mastery, the things that made you who you are, could be used to create a new, unique form of contribution—one that requires a different kind of value.",
      "source": "target",
